Scenario: Create internal account
	Testing the ability to create an internal project on Koroneiki that later gets synced to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Internal              | true                                 |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Notes                 | Additional account notes             |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I update a project with the code "KORONEKORONE" using the following values on the sandbox
	| Region   | US      |
	| Language | English |
	Then I should be able to view a project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and following values on the sandbox
	| Koroneiki Account Key | Obtain from project name      |
	| Project Name          | Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                  |
	| Tier                  | Regular                       |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki |
	| Additional Notes	    | Additional account notes      |
	When I go to the Project Details page on sandbox
	And I search for the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then the project details with the following values should be visible
	| Project Code    | KORONEKORONE |
	| Status          | APPROVED     |
	| Support Region  | US           |
	| Tier            | Regular      |
	When I go to the History tab
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "internal" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account   |
	| Update Date                 | Today           |
	| Update Field Name           | internal        |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A             |
	| Update Field New Value      | true            |
	And the history entry in position number "2" with the field value "name" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin               |
	| Update Summary              | Added Team                    |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | name                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Korone - ${staticProjectName} |

