Scenario: Update child account
	Testing the ability to update a child project on Koroneiki and having the changes synced to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Notes                 | Additional account notes             |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         |
	And I create a child account for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KCHILDKCHILD                         |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Description           | Test child account on koroneiki      |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-9012                         |
	| Name                  | Kchild - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Notes                 | Additional child account notes       |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-3456                         |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Region                | United States                        |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporatesubsidiary.com | 
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test" on the sandbox
	And I go to the OSB admin main page on the sandbox
	And I update a project with the code "KORONEKORONE" using the following values on the sandbox
	| Region   | US      |
	| Language | English |
	And I update a project with the code "KCHILDKCHILD" using the following values on the sandbox
	| Region   | US      |
	| Language | English |
	And I update a koroneiki account with the name "Kchild - ${staticProjectName}" to have the following values
	| Code                  | OCHILDOCHILD                           |
	| Description           | Test update child account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-4321                           |
	| Name                  | Ochild - ${staticProjectName}          |
	| Notes                 | Some more child account notes          |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-8765                           |
	| Region                | Japan                                  |
	| Status                | Pending                                |
	| Tier                  | Premier                                |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiupdatesubsidiary.com      |
	Then I should be able to view a project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and following values on the sandbox
	| Koroneiki Account Key | Obtain from project name      |
	| Project Name          | Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                  |
	| Tier                  | Regular                       |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki |
	| Additional Notes	    | Additional account notes      |
	And I should be able to view a project with the name "Ochild - ${staticProjectName}" and following values on the sandbox
	| Koroneiki Account Key | Obtain from project name               |
	| Project Name          | Ochild - ${staticProjectName}          |
	| Code                  | OCHILDOCHILD                           |
	| Tier                  | Premier                                |
	| Description           | Test update child account on koroneiki |
	| Additional Notes	    | Some more child account notes          |
	And I should not be able to view a project with the name "Kchild - ${staticProjectName}" on the sandbox
	When I go to the Project Details page on sandbox
	Then I should not be able to view the project in the Project Details index with the name "KChild - ${staticProjectName}"
	When I go to the Project Details page on sandbox
	And I search for the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then the project details with the following values should be visible
	| Project Code    | KORONEKORONE |
	| Status          | APPROVED     |
	| Support Region  | US           |
	| Tier            | Regular      |
	When I go to the Project Details page on sandbox
	And I go to the project with the name "Ochild - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then the project details with the following values should be visible
	| Project Code    | OCHILDOCHILD |
	| Status          | PENDING      |
	| Support Region  | US           |
	| Tier            | Premier      |
	When I go to the History tab
	And I generate the account ID value for "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I rename the first account id value
	And I generate the account ID value for "Ochild - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I rename the second account id value
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "name" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin               |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account                 |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | name                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Kchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "parentAccountId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin     |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account       |
	| Update Date                 | Today               |
	| Update Field Name           | parentAccountId     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId1} |
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "accountId" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin     |
	| Update Summary              | Added Account       |
	| Update Date                 | Today               |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId2} |
	And the history entry in position number "2" with the field value "name" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin               |
	| Update Summary              | Added Team                    |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | name                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Kchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	And the history entry in position number "3" with the field value "name" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin               |
	| Update Summary              | Updated Account               |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | name                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | Kchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Update Field New Value      | Ochild - ${staticProjectName} |
	And the history entry in position number "4" with the field value "name" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki Admin               |
	| Update Summary              | Updated Team                  |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | name                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | Kchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Update Field New Value      | Ochild - ${staticProjectName} |

